OK, I've finally finished the last in the series of the NetHack quest
artifacts fanart - the Staff.

What I'd like to do now is to make them into a calendar, and sell this.
Since NetHack is a free open source game, half of any profits made
would be donated to charity - the Electronic Frontier Foundation would
seem to be appropriate - since it's devoted to protecting free speech
online. It would kinda be rude to keep all the money myself :-P

However, I'm not sure of the legalities/rules/whatever on this.

The artwork is entirely my own. The concepts are my own. Most of the
names of the artifacts that inspired me are from mythology or are very
general (Scepter of Might, etc). However, obviously NetHack (as a name)
is not my own.

So, what would be the consensus on publishing such a calendar? Would it
be allowed? Devteam of NetHack, would I have your permission to publish
such a calendar using the name NetHack? Do I *need* permission in order
to publish the calendar (though it would be kinda rude to do it
without). Does the GPL apply, since I'm not using any code from
NetHack?

I am not a lawyer. I'm just your average British computer geek

Any advice/comments/thoughts on this would be greatly appreciated.
Speed would also be appreciated, since if it's going to be a 2007
calendar, now is definitely the time to get it ready to be done.

